Z||000000||maryjane||07-18-2001||08:59 PM||||Anybody know a source for lighted window switches for 84 with switches in ctr console? i've reads the article in The Cave but not sure I want to get that creative. Hoping to find some drop ins.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||07-19-2001||12:34 AM||||I doubt there are any drop in. <P>Keep in mind these switches have to be very heavy duty so allot of aftermarket switches are out. These circuits are not relay driven. the switch handles the full power of running the window. (As opposed to the power lock that is relay driven. You could put any nearly switch on that circuit. It only runs the relay.)<P>Bill spent quite allot of time on that. If there were drop in ones I think he would have found them. Nearly any switch you find is going to need some sort of alteration to be mounted there and to wire in.<P>You could salvage surf like Bill did and see what you come up with. There may be something that needs less cutting. Unless it comes from another GM it likely won't match the rest of the switches in the car. Bill's idea was to have the end result look OE.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||07-19-2001||01:10 AM||||Thanks,guess my best bet is to stay with the original ones. Bill's switch's look great, <BR>problem is, I don't see well enough to do meticulous work anymore. or maybe I could talk Jane into doing it.<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||07-19-2001||04:21 AM||||Here's some schematics that may help you. All you need is to wire in a relay in place of the stock switch connections, that will allow you to use any switch you like. I don't think I have the relay symbol right, but it should be fairly easy to decipher...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.escape.ca/~fogg/circuit.jpg"> <P>All you need is a power source (off the cig lighter circuit?) to drive the relay, and power the lit switch.||||reg||7
Z||000004||Bill Osmer||07-20-2001||01:50 PM||||Yes, you probably could use a lower voltage switch in conjunction with relay(S). Your schematic, howvever, does not match real-life window switches - the switch actually provides a reversing ability to the motors - this means that both connections to the window motors goes through the stock switches. If you upgrade your schematic to include more contacts in the relay or more relays, then the circuit might work with low voltage switches.<P>IMHO<P>Bill<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000005||theogre||07-21-2001||12:03 PM||||Relays would be as much work or more than the way Bill did it.<P>You'd need 4 double pole relays to replace the high curent switches. One up and one down relay for each window.<P>One relay gets wired stright thru. The other gets wired with the motor leads reveresed.||||reg||1
